  favorite lana laser beam ecot and sean  jacksepticeye mclaughlin who will be  voicing the iconic video game character  q bert  since that character speaks nearly  exclusively in bleeped curses this  should be interesting  what's he saying felix stand by my  kubernetes is a little rusty  the familiar faces don't end there  appearing in the main caster thor  ragnarok director taika waititi is video  game developer antoine  killing eaves jody coomer as programmer  millie and her in-game alter ego molotov  girl stranger things star joe kiri as  programmer keys  and get out actor lil raul howry is  guy's fellow npc  and friend buddy one thing we're  extremely curious about is who or what  will serve as the in-game big bad  while guy will be working against  external forces to keep his world from  collapsing it stands the reason that  i'll have some kind of virtual nemesis  to contend with as well  but as far as who or what that villain  could be we still don't know  the story of free guy has had a long  road to theaters even before the  pandemic delays  deadline reported back in 2016 that the  film back then described as a matt  lieberman spec script in the vein of the  truman show had acquired the highly  sought after deadpool star ryan reynolds  the overall plot seems to have remained  the same since then but given reynold's  star power and his love of getting  creatively involved in his projects it's  likely that the movie's tone evolved  from there to match his personality and  talents  and while reynolds wasn't one of the  initial creators of the project it's  clear that he fell deeply in love with  it  in 2019 he said i haven't been this  fully immersed and engaged in something  since deadpool  i think we live in really weird times  right now you're watching the news and  the top story today is  it's the end of the world i felt a  kinship to the character in that you can  sometimes feel like a background  character  the world is on loop and you have no  control over what's happening  that sounds like a fascinating theme to  explore through comedy and we're  intrigued to see how free guy tackles  the idea of an npc facing an existential  crisis  but beyond the broad themes and premise  we actually don't know much about the  movie's plot  although the trailers give us a good  idea of what to expect the first trailer  is  simply put gloriously bonkers set to the  bouncy strains of mariah carey's fantasy  it shows a look at a typical day in  guy's life  that leads to a snap decision to  suddenly involve himself in the mayhem  that results in his world turning upside  down and his reaction to his realization  that his world isn't exactly  you know real we also get an idea of the  excellent comedic chemistry between  reynolds and comer  along with an abundance of explosions  gunfights and wild stunts  it's not like ryan reynolds has a  conflicted history when it comes to  those sort of things  answer as quickly as you can now if you  had a gun to your head  the second trailer for free guy is just  as jam-packed with awesomeness as its  predecessor but offers a more concrete  sense in the movie's narrative guy is a  background character of a video game who  learns he isn't real  and ventures to become the hero of his  world and save it from impending doom  the third trailer places further  emphasis on the character of molotov  girl and the role she plays in the plot  it seems she will be instrumental in  guys development from clueless npc to  self-aware action hero  of course although there's a lot we can  figure out from the trailers there's a  lot more we don't know  in addition to our questions about the  movie's main villain we also wonder just  how jody comer's dual character will  figure in  she's been presented as an in-game ally  to guy but she's also one of the game's  programmers in the real world  with this in mind it sure seems like she  could have a key role to play in  convincing taika white tt's developer  character not to pull the plug on the  game  but beyond guy's gradual evolution into  a hero the details of the story of free  guy remain a mystery  that's probably a good thing as we feel  like this is going to be a flick that's  full of hilarious and inspired surprises  most likely the less you know the more  enjoyable it will all be  and based on the trailer so far we have  a solid idea of its overall vibe which  is every bit as hilarious as you would  hope for it to be  that's not huge jackman though no it  sure isn't that's like five foot nine  wolvie from the comics  yeah that's real wolverine yeah hugh  jackman kind of outdid himself never  heard of him  considering the video game themed plots  including a number of game references  cameos and more it goes without saying  that if there's a prime audience for  free guy it's the gaming community  there's so many callbacks to the games  that we know and love  you're going to be really excited to see  it however ryan reynolds has fans all  over the place some of whom may have  never even held a game controller  will these people get lost not according  to reynolds during a 2019 press  conference reynolds drew a comparison to  sports movies and how even people who  might have no interest in say  an actual baseball game can still be  thrilled by a baseball movie  in his words i always look at it like  sports movies are good metaphors  the greatest sports movies ever made are  not actually about sports  field of dreams i wouldn't characterize  that as a baseball story they used  baseball as a vehicle to tell a really  beautiful story about a son and a father  trying to connect  i think that we're doing the same thing  director sean levy added that the  movie's central conceit about an npc who  is just finding out that he is in a game  means that the ideal audience surrogate  is actually a non-gamer  a non-gaming audience will easily be  able to place themselves in guy's shoes  as he learns all about what video games  are and